---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Damage Control
description: "A private damage log for warehouse and delivery teams: damage rate, DPMO and sigma level, a Pareto of causes, where in the process damage happens, and a loading floor check."
activeNav: /tools.html
permalink: /tools/damage-control/
---
<section class="shell page-hero tool-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Free tool · Warehouse</p>
  <h1>Damage Control</h1>
  <p class="lede">Log every damaged unit with the stage where it was found and the cause behind it. The tool shows your damage rate, the few causes behind most of it, and where in the process to start.</p>
</section>

<section class="shell tool-layout dc-setup">
  <div class="tool-panel" data-damage-control>
    <fieldset class="dc-box">
      <legend class="kicker">1 · Period</legend>
      <div class="dc-grid">
        <div class="field dc-wide">
          <label for="dc-period">Period <span class="optional">optional</span></label>
          <input id="dc-period" name="period" placeholder="e.g. Week 38, outbound" autocomplete="off" data-setting>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="dc-volume">Units handled</label>
          <input id="dc-volume" name="volume" type="number" min="0" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="e.g. 18400" data-setting>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="dc-target">Target damage % <span class="optional">optional</span></label>
          <input id="dc-target" name="target" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 0.3" data-setting>
        </div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <form class="dc-box" data-entry>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="kicker">2 · Log a damage</legend>
        <div class="dc-grid">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="dc-date">Date</label>
            <input id="dc-date" name="date" type="date" required>
          </div>
          {%- for f in damageControl.fields %}
          <div class="field">
            <label for="dc-{{ f.name }}">{{ f.label }}</label>
            <select id="dc-{{ f.name }}" name="{{ f.name }}">
              {%- for option in f.options %}
              <option>{{ option }}</option>
              {%- endfor %}
            </select>
          </div>
          {%- endfor %}
          <div class="field">
            <label for="dc-units">Units damaged</label>
            <input id="dc-units" name="units" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" inputmode="numeric" required>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="dc-cost">Cost € <span class="optional">optional</span></label>
            <input id="dc-cost" name="cost" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal">
          </div>
          <div class="field dc-wide">
            <label for="dc-note">Note <span class="optional">optional</span></label>
            <input id="dc-note" name="note" placeholder="e.g. Cage 4, top layer collapsed" autocomplete="off">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-actions">
          <button class="button-primary" type="submit">Add to log</button>
          <p class="form-note" data-entry-status aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
      </fieldset>
    </form>

    <details class="dc-box dc-paste">
      <summary class="kicker">Or paste from Excel</summary>
      <p class="form-note">One row per damage, columns in this order: <strong>date, shift, stage, damage type, cause, units, cost, note</strong>. Tabs, semicolons or commas all work, and a header row is skipped. Your own stage or cause names are kept as they are.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="dc-paste">Rows to import</label>
        <textarea id="dc-paste" rows="5" placeholder="2026-09-14	Late	Loading	Crushed	Stacking	6	55"></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-actions">
        <button class="button-secondary" type="button" data-import>Import rows</button>
        <p class="form-note" data-import-status aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <div class="dc-box">
      <div class="dc-log-head">
        <p class="kicker">3 · Log</p>
        <p class="form-note" data-log-count></p>
      </div>
      <div class="dc-table-wrap" data-log-wrap hidden>
        <table class="dc-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Date</th>{% for f in damageControl.fields %}<th scope="col">{{ f.label }}</th>{% endfor %}<th scope="col" class="num">Units</th><th scope="col" class="num">€</th><th scope="col">Note</th><th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Remove</span></th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody data-log></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="dc-empty" data-log-empty>No damage logged yet. Add the first one above, paste from Excel, or <button class="button-ghost" type="button" data-example>load an example week</button>.</p>
      <div class="tool-actions">
        <button class="button-secondary" type="button" data-csv>Download CSV</button>
        <button class="button-secondary" type="button" data-clear>Clear log</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="tool-aside">
    <p class="kicker">How to use it</p>
    <ul class="tips">
      <li><strong>Log where it was found.</strong> The stage is where the damage was seen, the cause is why it happened. Both matter.</li>
      <li><strong>Count units, not incidents.</strong> Six crushed parcels from one collapsed wall are six units.</li>
      <li><strong>Add the volume.</strong> Without units handled you see counts; with them you get a rate, DPMO and sigma level.</li>
      <li><strong>Fix the vital few.</strong> Two or three causes usually carry most of the damage. Start there, then take the top one through <a class="inline-link" href="/tools/five-whys/">5 Whys</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="privacy-note">Your log stays in this browser. Nothing is sent or uploaded, and you can clear it at any time.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="shell dc-results" data-results tabindex="-1" hidden></section>

<section class="shell dc-check" data-floor-check>
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Floor check</p>
      <h2>Does the standard hold?</h2>
    </div>
    <p>Walk the dock and tick what you actually see today, not what the SOP says. Every unticked line is a place where damage can start.</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="dc-checklist">
    {%- for item in damageControl.checklist %}
    <li>
      <label class="dc-check-item">
        <input type="checkbox" name="check{{ loop.index0 }}">
        <span>{{ item }}</span>
      </label>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
  <div class="dc-check-foot">
    <p class="dc-score" data-check-score aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="tool-actions">
      <button class="button-secondary" type="button" data-check-reset>Reset the check</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/json" id="damage-control-data">{{ damageControl | dump | safe }}</script>
<script src="/js/damage-control.js" defer></script>
